      "assessment": {
        "nobel_worthiness": "Horizon-scale imaging made a black-hole shadow an observable object and opened a striking new regime of gravitational astrophysics.",
        "attribution": "These names represent the theoretical proposal, the long-baseline interferometry leadership, and the effort that brought the global array and imaging result together; the achievement depended on a very large collaboration.",
        "maturity": "The M87* and Sagittarius A* results provide powerful confirmation, while continued observations and improved imaging can refine the interpretation.",
        "uncertainties": [
